title: The European Union
subtitle: Use democratic institutions in opposition; negotiate Polish policy in government.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
frequency: 130
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_european_campaign_timer <= 0
call: poland_normalize
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_european_campaign_timer = 4; foreign_cards_resolved += 1; foreign_authority_last_issue = "European Union"
card-image: img/poland/cards/palace-mediation.webp

= The European Union

**Our position:** [+ foreign_authority_label +].
EU relationship **[+ eu_institutional_trust +]/100** · political influence
**[+ eu_influence +]/100** · progressive headwind **[+
eu_progressive_headwind +]/20** · Western economic access **[+
western_economic_access +]/100**.

[? if not left_in_government: PiS controls the Polish state channel. Lewica
can still use the European Parliament, Commission procedures, courts, sister
parties and public evidence to strengthen the democratic case inside Poland.?]
[? if left_in_government: Lewica now shares responsibility for the Polish
position. Party contacts still matter, but funds, Council bargains and
implementation belong to the cabinet.?]

- @democratic
- @social
- @settlement
- @confront

@democratic
title: [? if not left_in_government: Build the opposition's democratic channel?][? if left_in_government: Restore the government's institutional channel?]
subtitle: Courts, parliamentary scrutiny and published benchmarks—not bilateral theatre.
on-arrival: {!
const executive = Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government;
if (!Q.eu_brussels_mission) {
    Q.eu_brussels_mission = 1;
    Q.eu_campaign_progress += 1;
}
Q.eu_institutional_trust += executive ? 7 : 5;
Q.eu_influence += executive ? 4 : 3;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 3;
Q.foreign_pressure -= executive ? 3 : 1;
if (executive) {
    Q.government_delivery += 2;
    Q.foreign_policy_responsibility += 3;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome =
        "Cabinet publishes benchmarks and restores the EU institutional channel";
} else {
    Q.media_capacity += 2;
    Q.ko_relation += 2;
    Q.last_policy_stage = "European democratic advocacy";
    Q.last_policy_authority = "Opposition parties, MEPs and parliamentary committees";
    Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome =
        "Opposition evidence and European procedures strengthen the democratic case in Poland";
}
Q.news_headline = Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome;
!}

Benchmarks, filings and committee timetables are unglamorous, and they are the
only instruments that bind. The argument moves from who is offended to which
article was breached and by what date it will be repaired.

- #poland_card_finish

@social
title: Build a European coalition for wages, public services and equal rights
subtitle: Organise against the EU's rightward shift; this builds support but does not pass Polish law.
on-arrival: {!
const executive = Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government;
if (!Q.eu_social_mission) {
    Q.eu_social_mission = 1;
    Q.eu_campaign_progress += 1;
}
Q.eu_left_network += executive ? 7 : 6;
Q.eu_influence += executive ? 4 : 3;
Q.eu_progressive_headwind -= executive ? 4 : 2;
Q.labor_credibility += 3;
Q.abortion_reform_progress += 2;
Q.marriage_reform_progress += 2;
Q.labor_reform_progress += 2;
if (executive) {
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 2;
    Q.foreign_policy_responsibility += 2;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome =
        "Government recruits European allies for a social reform agenda";
} else {
    Q.last_policy_stage = "European coalition building";
    Q.last_policy_authority = "Lewica, trade unions and sister parties";
    Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome =
        "Lewica gives the opposition's European case a social programme";
}
Q.news_headline = Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome;
!}

Sister parties, federations and a shared programme give the Polish Left
something it usually lacks: allies arguing the same case in their own
parliaments. It moves no Polish bill by itself, and it changes what a Polish
bill can count on when it moves.

- #poland_card_finish

@settlement
title: Negotiate a Polish settlement on funds, law and social investment
subtitle: Government only. Requires both European channels and EU trust of at least 38.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and eu_campaign_complete = 0
choose-if: government_has_confidence = 1 and eu_brussels_mission = 1 and eu_social_mission = 1 and eu_institutional_trust >= 38
unavailable-subtitle: The cabinet first needs a democratic channel, a social coalition and enough institutional trust.
on-arrival: eu_campaign_complete = 1; eu_influence += 8; eu_institutional_trust += 8; eu_progressive_headwind -= 3; economic_growth += 0.3; government_delivery += 5; foreign_pressure -= 5; foreign_policy_responsibility += 5; foreign_authority_last_outcome = "Government secures a Polish EU settlement and restores economic access"; news_headline = foreign_authority_last_outcome

European money and legal commitments move together again. The agreement does
not make Brussels progressive; it gives Polish reforms allies, funding and a
published route through institutions that can still say no.

- #poland_card_finish

@confront
title: Align with the sovereignty camp and confront the EU
subtitle: The rhetoric is usable immediately; colder relations can later reach growth and jobs.
on-arrival: {!
const executive = Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.pis_relation += 3;
Q.hungary_fidesz_channel += executive ? 4 : 2;
Q.eu_institutional_trust -= executive ? 9 : 5;
Q.eu_influence -= executive ? 6 : 3;
Q.eu_progressive_headwind += 2;
Q.foreign_pressure += executive ? 5 : 2;
Q.far_right_agenda += 2;
if (executive) {
    Q.foreign_policy_responsibility += 6;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome =
        "Cabinet joins the sovereignty camp and accepts the economic risk";
} else {
    Q.media_capacity += 2;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome =
        "Opposition rhetoric attacks Brussels without withdrawing Poland from any agreement";
}
Q.news_headline = Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome;
!}

The lines are good and they travel. Poland's negotiators then arrive at the
next Council table with less to trade and a reputation that precedes them,
which is a bill that falls due long after the applause.

- #poland_card_finish
